{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of 6-K-EX-99.1_2026-11-05_genmabinterimreportq32026.htm, sha256 101152228ad8794ed8d03c1dcb58926428aca62893f0a5b208e241c3c568aa71.\nEX-99.1 2 genmabinterimreportq32026.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 Genmab Announces Financial Results for the Nine Months of 2026\nNovember 5, 2026 Copenhagen, Denmark; Interim Report for the Nine Months Ended September 30, 2026\nHighlights\n\u2022Epcoritamab approved in Europe (as TEPKINLY\u00ae) and Japan (as EPKINLY\u00ae) in combination with R\u00b2 for the treatment of adult patients with relapsed or refractory FL \u2022Initiation of two new Phase 3 trials for petosemtamab in first- and second-line CRC \u2022Genmab revenue increased 22% compared to the first nine months of 2025, to $3,238 million\n\u201cThe third quarter of 2026 reinforced the breadth of our late-stage portfolio. TEPKINLY plus R2 became the first bispecific-based therapy approved in Europe for second-line FL, extending epcoritamab's reach as a core therapy across B-cell malignancies. We also broadened our petosemtamab program with new Phase 3 studies in CRC, underscoring our confidence in this asset beyond head and neck cancer. As anticipated, we are now in our data-rich fourth quarter, where we have delivered pivotal readouts across our three late-stage assets, epcoritamab, Rina-S\u00ae (rinatabart sesutecan) and petosemtamab, supporting multiple regulatory submissions and potential launches in 2027,\u201d said Jan van de Winkel, Ph.D., Chief Executive Officer of Genmab.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Financial Performance First Nine Months of 2026 \u2022Revenue was $3,238 million for the first nine months of 2026 compared to $2,662 million for the first nine months of 2025. The increase of $576 million, or 22%, was primarily driven by higher DARZALEX\u00ae and Kesimpta\u00ae royalties and higher EPKINLY\u00ae net product sales. \u2022Royalty revenue was $2,699 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $2,219 million in the first nine months of 2025, an increase of $480 million, or 22%. The increase in royalties was driven by higher net sales of DARZALEX and Kesimpta. \u2022Net sales of DARZALEX by J&J were $12,410 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $10,448 million in the first nine months of 2025, an increase of $1,962 million or 19%. \u2022Global net sales of EPKINLY/TEPKINLY\u00ae were $491 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $333 million in the first nine months of 2025, an increase of $158 million or 47%. \u2022Cost of product sales were $234 million for the first nine months of 2026 compared to $157 million for the first nine months of 2025. The increase of $77 million, or 49%, was primarily driven by the profit-sharing amounts payable to AbbVie related to EPKINLY sales. \u2022Acquisition and integration related charges related to the integration of Merus were $87 million in the first nine months of 2026. \u2022Amortization of acquired intangible assets was $35 million for the first nine months of 2026 compared to $9 million for the first nine months of 2025. The increase of $26 million, was primarily driven by the amortization of the Merus technology platform. \u2022Operating expenses were $2,018 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $1,498 million in the first nine months of 2025, an increase of $520 million or 35%. \u2022Adjusted operating expenses, which exclude Acquisition and integration related charges and Amortization of acquired intangible assets, were $1,896 million for the first nine months of 2026 compared to $1,489 million for the first nine months of 2025. The increase of $407 million, or 27%, was primarily driven by investment in our product pipeline, including the advancement of Rina-S and petosemtamab, and our global commercialization capabilities in preparation for their anticipated launches. \u2022Operating profit was $986 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $1,007 million in the first nine months of 2025. Adjusted operating profit, which excludes Acquisition and integration related charges and Amortization of acquired intangible assets, was $1,108 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $1,016 million in the first nine months of 2025.\nNon-IFRS Financial Measures Our Adjusted operating expenses and adjusted operating profit excludes acquisition and integration related charges and amortization of acquired intangible assets. These charges were recognized in current as well as prior periods and will likely reoccur in future periods. These items are excluded from operating expenses and\nGenmab A/S\n"}
