{"page": 4, "text": "* Acquisition and integration related charges ** Amortization of intangible assets acquired through acquisitions ***Includes all expenses presented within Total costs and operating expenses, less cost of product sales. Key Company Events Post-Quarter End \u2022October: Positive topline results from the Phase 3 EPCORE\u00ae DLBCL-2 trial evaluating fixed treatment duration epcoritamab in combination with standard of care rituximab, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin hydrochloride, vincristine, and prednisone (R-CHOP), compared to R-CHOP alone, in newly diagnosed patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) with an International Prognostic Index (IPI) score of 2 to 5. Data will be submitted for presentation at a future medical meeting. Genmab and AbbVie Inc. (AbbVie) will engage global regulatory authorities to determine next steps. \u2022October: Positive topline results from the global Phase 3 RAINFOL\u2122-02 trial of Rina-S in patients with platinum-resistant ovarian cancer (PROC) regardless of Folate Receptor Alpha (FR\u03b1) expression level or prior treatment with mirvetuximab. The trial met its primary endpoint of progression-free survival (PFS), with Rina-S demonstrating a statistically significant and clinically meaningful improvement compared with investigator\u2019s choice chemotherapy in the intent-to-treat (ITT) and in the primary analysis set (PAS) populations. Based on these results, Genmab plans to engage with regulatory authorities worldwide regarding potential next steps. The data will also be submitted for presentation at a future medical meeting. \u2022October: Positive topline results from the global Phase 3 LiGeR-HN1 trial (NCT06525220) evaluating petosemtamab in combination with pembrolizumab versus pembrolizumab in patients with first-line (1L) PD-L1 positive recurrent/metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC). The trial met both of its primary endpoints of overall survival (OS) and objective response rate (ORR), regardless of HPV status. Based on these positive topline results, Genmab plans to engage global regulatory authorities and will submit the full results from LiGeR-HN1 for presentation at a future medical meeting.\nOutlook\nGenmab is maintaining its 2026 financial guidance published August 6, 2026.\nConference Call\nGenmab will hold a conference call to discuss the results for the first nine months of 2026 today, Thursday, November 5, at 6:00 pm CET, 5:00 pm GMT or 12:00 pm EST. To join the call please use the below registration link. Registered participants will receive an email with a link to access dial-in information as well as a unique\nGenmab A/S\nCarl Jacobsens Vej 30\n2500 Valby, Denmark Tel: +45 7020 2728 www.genmab.com Company Announcement no. 45 Page 2/45 CVR no. 2102 3884\n"}
