2025, were $87 million in the first nine months of 2026. There were no acquisition and integration related charges in the first nine months of 2025. Key Developments to Acquisition and Integration Related Charges \u2013 Third Quarter of 2026 Acquisition and integration related charges, which related primarily to severance, retention and professional fees incurred in connection with the integration of Merus following its acquisition in December 2025, were $10 million for the third quarter of 2026. There were no acquisition and integration related charges for the third quarter of 2025. Amortization of Acquired Intangible Assets\n"}
{"page": 25, "text": "Amortization of acquired intangible assets, which includes amortization of technology platform and commercialized intangible assets acquired through acquisitions, was $35 million for the first nine months of 2026 compared to $9 million for the first nine months of 2025. The increase of $26 million was primarily driven by the amortization of the Merus technology platform and commercialized intangible asset acquired in December 2025. Key Developments to Amortization of Acquired Intangible Assets \u2013 Third Quarter of 2026 Amortization of acquired intangible assets was $11 million for the third quarter of 2026 compared to $3 million for the third quarter of 2025. The increase of $8 million, was primarily driven by the amortization of the Merus technology platform acquired in December 2025. Operating Profit\nOperating profit was $986 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $1,007 million in the first nine months of 2025. The decrease was driven by the items described above. Adjusted operating profit excluding Acquisition and integration related charges and Amortization of acquired intangible assets, was $1,108 million in the first nine months of 2026 compared to $1,016 million in the first nine months of 2025. Key Developments to Operating Profit - Third Quarter of 2026\nOperating profit was $431 million for the third quarter of 2026 compared to $459 million for the third quarter of 2025. The decrease was driven by the items described above. Adjusted operating profit excluding Acquisition and integration related charges and Amortization of acquired intangible assets, was $452 million in the third quarter of 2026 compared to $462 million in the third quarter of 2025.\nGenmab A/S\nCarl Jacobsens Vej 30\n2500 Valby, Denmark Tel: +45 7020 2728 www.genmab.com Company Announcement no. 45 Page 20/45 CVR no. 2102 3884\nInterim Report for the Nine Months of 2026 Net Financial Items\nFinancial income and expense was comprised of the following: